:: Widgets Fishing Magnet Catch [widget]
<<widget "fishingMagnetCatchText">>
	<<set _magnetLoot to _args[0]>>
	<<set _fishingWaterBody to fishingLocationWaterBodyName($bus)>>
	The line tugs as the magnet snags something below. You reel it in and lift <<a _magnetLoot.name>> dripping out of the <<= _fishingWaterBody>>,
	<<switch _magnetLoot.type>>
		<<case "rustedCan">>
			water sloshing out of the hole in its side.
		<<case "wireTangle">>
			knotted and awkward to work free from the magnet.
		<<case "chainLength">>
			flaking rust onto your hands as you pull it clear.
		<<case "horseshoe">>
			crusted with rust and worn smooth on one side.
		<<case "bikeWheel">>
			its spokes bent and tangled with weed.
		<<case "numberPlate">>
			caked in silt and long stripped of paint.
		<<case "kitchenKnife">>
			the blade pitted with rust.
		<<case "padlock">>
			still locked, its shackle orange with rust.
		<<case "toolbox">>
			the latch long since seized shut.

		<<case "lostKeys">>
			still looped on a rotted length of cord.
		<<case "screwdriver">>
			the handle bare wood, the tip gone to rust.
		<<case "forceps">>
			the jaws locked open, thick with corrosion.
		<<case "drillBits">>
			clinking together as you pull them free.
		<<case "pliers">>
			the grip cracked and the jaws seized shut.
		<<case "silverCutlery">>
			crusted with silt, but the silver still gleams underneath.
		<<default>>
			<<error { message: "fishingMagnetCatchText: unknown magnet loot key: " + _magnetLoot.type }>>
	<</switch>>
<</widget>>
